From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:48:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] feat(scripts): generate a derived locale's
 art-availability sidecar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ships the measurement the printing preference depends on. Without it a clone has
no sidecar, the client finds no availability for the locale, and the feature
silently does nothing — so it has to be a checked-in script, not a one-off.

Two CDN rules are encoded because both cost a silent wrong answer if missed: GET
rather than HEAD (it 404s HEAD on an object absent from its edge cache and 200s
the same URL to GET, so a HEAD run reports ~0% coverage and looks fine), and
`Range: bytes=0-0` to keep a probe to one byte. Probes that fail after retries are
recorded separately and warned about, never folded into "absent", so a network
blip cannot quietly drop a printing that does have art.

Scoping is by set code, so a single-product channel measures only its own pool:
Doctor Who's 1178 printings in ~15s, 398 of them (33%) with art.
